{
  "concept": "The circular sector of angle x is geometrically trapped between an inner right triangle (area sin x / 2) and an outer right triangle (area tan x / 2), giving sin x / 2 <= x / 2 <= tan x / 2, the sandwich that forces lim_{x->0} sin x / x = 1.",
  "figureType": "diagram",
  "elements": [
    "left panel: horizontal x-axis and vertical y-axis through the origin",
    "left panel: blue unit circle centered at the origin",
    "left panel: angle arc labeled x at the origin between the positive x-axis and the radius",
    "left panel: red radius line from origin to the point (cos x, sin x) on the circle",
    "left panel: red dot at (1, 0) on the x-axis, labeled '(1, 0)'",
    "left panel: red dot at (cos x, sin x) on the circle, labeled '(cos x, sin x)'",
    "left panel: vertical red dashed tangent line at x = 1 from (1,0) up to (1, tan x)",
    "left panel: red dot at (1, tan x), labeled '(1, tan x)'",
    "left panel: red solid line from origin to (1, tan x) (the extended radius / hypotenuse of the big triangle)",
    "left panel: red dashed chord from (cos x, sin x) to (1, 0)",
    "left panel: horizontal brace under the segment from 0 to 1 labeled '1'",
    "right panel 1: outer right triangle, base 1, vertical height tan x, light pink fill, red edges, with a blue dashed unit arc inside, side brace labeled 'tan x', caption 'Area of triangle' and formula 'tan x / 2'",
    "right panel 2: circular sector of angle x and radius 1, light pink fill, red radial edges, blue arc, caption 'Area of sector' and formula 'x / 2'",
    "right panel 3: inner right triangle, base 1, vertical height sin x, light pink fill, red edges, red dashed altitude, blue dashed arc on the hypotenuse side, side brace labeled 'sin x', caption 'Area of triangle' and formula 'sin x / 2'",
    "right panels: angle arc labeled x at each triangle/sector vertex",
    "right panels: base labels '1' under each shape",
    "two '>=' inequality symbols placed between the three area captions and repeated between the three formulas"
  ],
  "interactions": [
    {
      "id": "angleX",
      "type": "slider",
      "label": "Angle x",
      "range": [0.05, 1.55, 0.01],
      "default": 0.9,
      "teaches": "At every angle the inner triangle stays inside the sector and the sector stays inside the outer triangle, so the inequality sin x / 2 <= x / 2 <= tan x / 2 is not a coincidence at one angle but a fact for all x in (0, pi/2)"
    },
    {
      "id": "viewMode",
      "type": "toggle",
      "label": "Layout",
      "options": ["Side-by-side", "Overlaid"],
      "default": "Side-by-side",
      "teaches": "Overlaying the three shapes on one origin reveals the actual reason for the inequality: the small triangle is contained in the sector, which is contained in the big triangle, so their areas must be ordered the same way"
    },
    {
      "id": "highlightRegion",
      "type": "button",
      "label": "Highlight region (click a caption)",
      "states": ["none", "outerTriangle", "sector", "innerTriangle"],
      "default": "none",
      "teaches": "Clicking a caption isolates one region and surfaces its area formula, letting the learner read off tan x / 2, x / 2, and sin x / 2 one at a time and see which bound each provides"
    }
  ],
  "demo_steps": [
    {
      "title": "Three areas, one angle",
      "narration": "For a fixed angle x the figure builds three shapes from the unit circle: a big right triangle of height tan x, the sector of angle x, and a small right triangle of height sin x. Their areas are tan x / 2, x / 2, and sin x / 2.",
      "state": { "viewMode": "Side-by-side", "highlightRegion": "none", "angleX": 0.9 }
    },
    {
      "title": "See the containment",
      "narration": "Switch to the overlaid view: the small triangle sits inside the sector, and the sector sits inside the big triangle. Because area respects containment, sin x / 2 <= x / 2 <= tan x / 2 follows immediately.",
      "state": { "viewMode": "Overlaid", "highlightRegion": "none", "angleX": 0.9 }
    },
    {
      "title": "Read the upper bound",
      "narration": "Highlight the outer triangle to surface its area tan x / 2 — this is the largest of the three and gives the upper bound on the sector's area x / 2.",
      "state": { "viewMode": "Overlaid", "highlightRegion": "outerTriangle", "angleX": 0.9 }
    },
    {
      "title": "Read the lower bound",
      "narration": "Highlight the inner triangle to surface its area sin x / 2 — the smallest of the three, giving the lower bound on x / 2.",
      "state": { "viewMode": "Overlaid", "highlightRegion": "innerTriangle", "angleX": 0.9 }
    },
    {
      "title": "Squeeze as x shrinks",
      "narration": "Drag the angle toward 0: both bounding triangles collapse onto the sector, so tan x / 2 and sin x / 2 both approach x / 2. Dividing the sandwich by sin x / 2 yields cos x <= sin x / x <= 1 / cos x, and the Squeezing Theorem gives the limit 1.",
      "state": { "viewMode": "Overlaid", "highlightRegion": "none", "angleX": 0.15 }
    }
  ],
  "keyInsight": "The inequality is purely geometric: the sector is sandwiched between two triangles that contain and are contained by it, so its area x / 2 is trapped between sin x / 2 and tan x / 2 — and that trap tightens to a single value as x -> 0.",
  "reconstructionNotes": "Two-zone layout. Left zone: black coordinate axes, a bold blue unit circle, a red radius to (cos x, sin x), a red vertical dashed tangent at x=1 rising to (1, tan x), red dots and italic serif labels for (1,0), (cos x, sin x), (1, tan x), a small angle arc labeled x at the origin, and a brace labeled 1 under the unit base. Right zone in side-by-side mode: three light-pink-filled shapes in a row separated by '>=' symbols — outer right triangle (vertical side braced 'tan x'), blue-arc sector, inner right triangle (vertical side braced 'sin x') — each with an angle arc x, a base label 1, a caption ('Area of triangle' / 'Area of sector' / 'Area of triangle') and a stacked fraction formula (tan x / 2, x / 2, sin x / 2). In overlaid mode draw all three concentrically at a single origin (inner triangle inside sector inside outer triangle) so containment is visible; keep the same pink fill, red edges, and blue arcs, dimming non-highlighted regions when highlightRegion is set. The slider drives the angle in both zones simultaneously; keep the left circle's geometry and the right shapes' heights (tan x, sin x) consistent with the slider value."
}

